  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider two&nbsp;spheres&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of the same size and made of the same material. The sphere&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is hollow while&nbsp;the&nbsp;sphere&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is solid. If both the spheres are heated to the same temperature, then</p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
